.TH PYLOADER 8 2026-10-25 DarqOS "DarqOS System Manager's Manual"
.SH NAME
pyloader \- DarqOS loader for Python executables
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pyloader
.I p-kernel-port dpid parent-dpid executable-path
.br
.B pyloader
.RB { help | \-h | \-? | \-\-help }
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pyloader
runs a Python executable as a DarqOS process.
It is normally started by
.BR pkernel (8)
in response to a
.B spawn_process
p-call, and is not meant to be run by hand.
.PP
.B pyloader
connects to the p-kernel on the loopback interface at
.IR p-kernel-port ,
sends a RUNNING message for
.IR dpid ,
then imports
.I main.py
from
.I executable-path
and calls its
.B darq_main()
function, with no arguments, on a new application thread.
.PP
The main thread runs an event loop that carries p-calls from the
application thread to the p-kernel and delivers the replies.
The process's
.B getpid()
and
.B getppid()
are answered locally from
.I dpid
and
.IR parent-dpid .
.PP
The host process title is set to
.BI darq- dpid
to make it easy to find with
.BR ps (1).
.SS Termination
.B pyloader
exits when the application's
.B darq_main()
returns, or when the p-kernel delivers a
.B kill_process
for this dpid.
A killed application thread is stopped by raising
.B SystemExit
in it; any p-call it is blocked in is abandoned.
If the thread does not stop (for example, because it is stuck in
native code),
.B pyloader
exits immediately with status 1.
.PP
If the p-kernel closes the connection, for instance because it does
not recognise
.IR dpid ,
.B pyloader
logs
.RB \(lq "Disconnected by p-kernel: exiting." \(rq,
stops the application, and exits with status 1.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I p-kernel-port
TCP port on which the p-kernel is listening.
.TP
.I dpid
DarqOS process identifier allocated to this process by the p-kernel.
.TP
.I parent-dpid
DarqOS process identifier of the process that requested the spawn, or
0 if it was started by the p-kernel itself.
.TP
.I executable-path
Directory containing the application's
.I main.py
file.
It is added to the front of the module search path.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PYTHONPATH
Must allow the
.B darq
package to be imported.
.BR pkernel (8)
sets this when it spawns the loader.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
0
The application finished, or was killed by
.BR kill_process .
.TP
1
The p-kernel closed the connection, the application thread could not
be stopped, or usage help was requested.
.TP
42
The wrong number of arguments was given.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Log messages are written to standard error.
.SH BUGS
If no p-kernel is listening on
.IR p-kernel-port ,
.B pyloader
exits with a Python traceback rather than an error message.
.PP
Asking for usage help exits with status 1.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pkernel (8)
